# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
#
# This file is committed. .env.local and every other .env file is not, which is
# the arrangement that lets a new person set the project up without ever seeing
# a real secret. Every variable the app reads should appear here, even before it
# is used anywhere.

# The public address of the deployed site. Safe to expose in the browser, since
# it ends up in the address bar anyway.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Everything below this line is server-only.
#
# Nothing prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ is ever a secret. Next.js compiles those
# into the JavaScript the browser downloads, where anyone can read them. If a
# key must stay private, it must not carry that prefix, and it must not be read
# from a component that runs in the browser.
#
# There is no backend yet, so these are placeholders for the names the app will
# need. Fill them in when the first endpoint is written.
# DATABASE_URL=
# SESSION_SECRET=
